# {{ package_name }}

Generated Terraform Plugin Framework models for `{{ sdk_import }}` at
`{{ sdk_version }}`. Requires Go 1.24 or later. Run `go mod tidy` to resolve
module dependencies after generation.

The SDK remains independent of Terraform. Provider builders own this module,
its generation configuration, and the resource/data-source implementations.
Use the same OpenAPI/IR and Arvalez version as the SDK, with the standard Go
model templates. No Terraform annotations are required in the service's API.

## Usage

For an SDK model `Widget`, the generated functions are `WidgetFromAPI`,
`WidgetToAPI`, `WidgetAttributeTypes`, `WidgetResourceAttributes`, and
`WidgetDataSourceAttributes`. Named enums have scalar models and conversions.

```go
// In a provider Schema method:
attrs, diags := tfmodels.WidgetResourceAttributes(ctx, tfmodels.SchemaOptions{
    Fields: map[string]tfmodels.FieldOptions{
        "name": {Role: tfmodels.Required},
    },
})
resp.Diagnostics.Append(diags...)
resp.Schema = schema.Schema{Attributes: attrs}

// In Read, after your SDK call:
model, diags := tfmodels.WidgetFromAPI(ctx, apiResponse)
resp.Diagnostics.Append(diags...)
if resp.Diagnostics.HasError() { return }
// Reconcile configured attributes before writing state if the API normalizes
// them. A nil API response is not an instruction to remove a resource.
if model != nil { resp.Diagnostics.Append(resp.State.Set(ctx, model)...) }

// In Create/Update, after req.Plan.Get into the appropriate request model:
request, diags := tfmodels.NewWidgetToAPI(ctx, &plan)
resp.Diagnostics.Append(diags...)
if resp.Diagnostics.HasError() { return }
// Pass request to your SDK operation's input struct.
```

These snippets illustrate model names; use the names generated from your API.
Nested `FieldOptions.Fields` apply to an object, or every object in a list/map.
Both schema helpers default every attribute to Computed. Resource options also
support OptionalComputed. Set `Sensitive` with a bool pointer. Helpers return
fresh maps, allowing provider-specific validators and plan modifiers to be
added. Field names and types must continue to match the models.

Conversions process all model fields independently of schema roles. Unknown
values anywhere in an outbound request produce diagnostics, never empty values.
Use SDK request models for writes. `FromAPI` performs structural conversion,
not lifecycle or plan/state reconciliation. Provider code owns CRUD, IDs,
imports, replacement rules, timeouts, API normalization, and error handling.

## Null and complex values

API omission and explicit JSON null both become Terraform null. Optional SDK
fields are omitted on reverse conversion by default. For an optional nullable
field, `null_behavior = "explicit_null"` sends JSON null instead; required
nullable fields always use the SDK's explicit-null representation. Required
non-nullable fields reject Terraform null. Nil and empty collections remain
distinct in memory, subject to the SDK's JSON omission rules.

Unions, free-form JSON, tuples, and recursive edges require explicit field
configuration in the generator:

```toml
[target.terraform.models.Widget.fields.payload]
representation = "json"

[target.terraform.models.Widget.fields.displayName]
name = "display_name"
null_behavior = "explicit_null" # only for optional nullable SDK fields
```

JSON strings must contain one value representable by the SDK type without data
loss. Unknown object fields, truncated fixed arrays, and trailing JSON are
rejected. Use Terraform null, not the JSON string `"null"`, for absent values.
JSON numbers retain precision through `json.Number` when the SDK uses `any`.
Default attribute names are snake_case; reserved Terraform names use `_value`.
Generation reports collisions so you can specify explicit `name` overrides.

## Local SDK development

Keep the generated `go.mod` portable. In a parent development directory, use
`go work init ./sdk ./tfmodels ./provider` (adjust paths) to develop the SDK,
adapters, and provider together without publishing. Do not commit a
machine-specific replacement into this generated module.

Regenerate adapters when the SDK model contract changes. Generation does not
install dependencies or change the SDK. Tera templates can be dumped and
overridden through Arvalez's Terraform template commands.

Nullability follows the shared IR and the SDK representation. Both OpenAPI 3.0
`type: string` with `nullable: true` and OpenAPI 3.1 `type: ["string", "null"]`
produce nullable SDK fields and Terraform conversions. In OpenAPI 3.0, declare
`nullable` alongside an explicit `type`; for a `$ref`, put it on the referenced
schema. Required nullable fields use `Nullable[T]`; optional nullable fields use
`*Nullable[T]` to distinguish omission from explicit null. Regenerate both the
SDK and adapters when adopting nullable declarations.
